    <sectiondef kind="func">
      <memberdef kind="function" id="_marmot_monomial_basis_functions_8h_1ad1defbf9b7b712fe1dc097ba48edc70b" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int Marmot::Math::computeSizeOfMonomialBasisVector</definition>
        <argsstring>(int order, int dim)</argsstring>
        <name>computeSizeOfMonomialBasisVector</name>
        <qualifiedname>Marmot::Math::computeSizeOfMonomialBasisVector</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>order</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>dim</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Compute the size of the complete monomial basis of a given order. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Computes the size of the H vector based on the completeness order and the dimension, cf. Eq. (3.67) in the book by Belytschko, Chen, Hillman, i.e., the number of monomials <formula id="85">$ \boldsymbol{x}^{\boldsymbol{\alpha}} $</formula> with <formula id="86">$ |\boldsymbol{\alpha}| \le n $</formula> in <formula id="87">$ d $</formula> dimensions, <formula id="88">$ \binom{d + n}{d} $</formula>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">order</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Completeness order <formula id="89">$ n $</formula> (zero for a negative order). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">dim</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Spatial dimension <formula id="90">$ d \ge 1 $</formula>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The number of monomials. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
